&lt;p&gt;The feature matrix lists environments under the Enterprise plan. Layer5 Cloud does not refuse environment actions because of the plan.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Meshery Server Registration</title><link>/pr-preview/pr-1343/cloud/concepts/meshery-server-registration/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/pr-preview/pr-1343/cloud/concepts/meshery-server-registration/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Layer5 Cloud is a &lt;a href="https://docs.meshery.io/extensibility/providers"&gt;Meshery remote provider&lt;/a&gt;. When a Meshery Server uses Layer5 Cloud, hosted or self-hosted, the server registers itself with Cloud on behalf of the signed-in user. Registration is what makes that Meshery Server known to Cloud: it appears as a &lt;code&gt;meshery&lt;/code&gt; connection owned by that user. This page explains what the server sends, how Cloud tells a new server from one it already knows, what survives re-registration, and what each failure means.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Integrations</title><link>/pr-preview/pr-1343/cloud/guides/integrations/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>/pr-preview/pr-1343/cloud/guides/integrations/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Integrations connect Layer5 Cloud to systems outside it. Today that means GitHub, for importing infrastructure files and posting pull-request snapshots, and the infrastructure connections that Meshery Servers register. This page lists every integration the product offers, what each one does, and where to configure it, so you can tell quickly whether Layer5 Cloud can connect to the tool you use.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2 id="integration-matrix" class="heading-link"&gt;
 Integration matrix
 &lt;a href="#integration-matrix" class="heading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink to this heading"&gt;🔗&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
 &lt;thead&gt;
 &lt;tr&gt;
 &lt;th&gt;Integration&lt;/th&gt;
 &lt;th&gt;What it does&lt;/th&gt;
 &lt;th&gt;Where to start&lt;/th&gt;
 &lt;/tr&gt;
 &lt;/thead&gt;
 &lt;tbody&gt;
 &lt;tr&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;GitHub (Layer5 GitHub App)&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Reads the repositories you grant, imports Kubernetes manifests, Helm charts, Docker Compose files, and Meshery designs as private designs, and can commit a snapshot workflow to a repository.&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;&lt;a href="/pr-preview/pr-1343/cloud/guides/integrations/github-integration/"&gt;Connect GitHub&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;/tr&gt;
 &lt;tr&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;GitHub Actions (Kanvas Snapshot)&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Posts a picture of your infrastructure on every pull request.&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;&lt;a href="/pr-preview/pr-1343/cloud/guides/integrations/github-actions/"&gt;Use GitHub Actions&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;/tr&gt;
 &lt;tr&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Meshery Server&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Registers each Meshery Server as a connection, so you can see and manage the servers in your organization.&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Listed under Meshery on the Integrations tab.&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;/tr&gt;
 &lt;tr&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Kubernetes&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Lists the clusters your Meshery Servers manage, so you can assign them to environments.&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;&lt;a href="/pr-preview/pr-1343/cloud/guides/workspaces/managing-environments/"&gt;Manage Environments&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;/tr&gt;
 &lt;tr&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Prometheus&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Lists Prometheus connections that Meshery Servers report.&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;td&gt;Listed under Prometheus on the Integrations tab.&lt;/td&gt;
 &lt;/tr&gt;
 &lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Meshery Servers register Meshery, Kubernetes, and Prometheus connections. Layer5 Cloud has no setup wizard for them. The Integrations tab shows what the servers in your organization registered, and you assign those connections to environments to decide which teams reach them.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>